<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Quantum rating upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Quantum rating upgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Gruntal and Co said Wednesday it upgraded its rating on Quantum Corp to outperform from neutral based on record shipments and record sales.</p>
<p>-- Gruntal also increased its estimate for Quantum's fiscal 1997 earnings to $1.61 from $0.83 and increasing the 1998 estimate to $3.39 from $2.20.</p>
<p>-- Quantum reported higher than expected third quarter earnings after the close yesterday, Gruntal said, posting revenues of $1.48 billion compared to $1.2 billion one year ago.</p>
<p>-- Quantum makes disk drives and related products.</p>
<p>-- Its shares were trading up 3-1/4 Wednesday at 36-3/8</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
